1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Let's go! You can do it, Kuribayashi!

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Come on, show him what experience made of!

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Visualize it.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
What I'd be doing in his place.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
I'd be more grateful to be there than that guy.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The jealousy is real, my friends.

7
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:55,348
Kuribayashi, take it away!

8
00:01:56,448 --> 00:01:57,888
Fast pressing by Tosu.

9
00:01:58,748 --> 00:02:00,608
Watch out! He's gonna tackle you!

10
00:02:07,768 --> 00:02:09,068
He passed him!

11
00:02:09,608 --> 00:02:12,888
Just when you thought he was in danger, Kuribayashi pulled out.

12
00:02:13,288 --> 00:02:17,348
He took advantage of the other player's momentum, and then he mowed right past him.

13
00:02:17,788 --> 00:02:19,028
A blindsiding move.

14
00:02:19,728 --> 00:02:21,028
You were one step behind.

15
00:02:21,028 --> 00:02:24,828
Tension's kind of different while watching on TV than it would be on the field.

16
00:02:25,128 --> 00:02:27,368
Takes more focus to imagine in real time.

17
00:02:27,588 --> 00:02:28,268
Stop talking!

18
00:02:30,748 --> 00:02:31,868
He's fast.

19
00:02:32,388 --> 00:02:34,088
He's definitely got the speed.

20
00:02:34,588 --> 00:02:36,628
I'd dribble past another if I were him.

21
00:02:37,188 --> 00:02:37,368
Huh?

22
00:02:37,988 --> 00:02:38,828
Oh, wow.

23
00:02:39,228 --> 00:02:40,228
There's the triangle!

24
00:02:40,528 --> 00:02:42,248
Those two guys just came over to cover.

25
00:02:42,628 --> 00:02:44,708
They can help him shake off that creeper dude.

26
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:48,328
Okay. It looks like Kuribayashi is choosing to pass.

27
00:02:48,328 --> 00:02:50,308
What did I say when I tell you?

28
00:02:50,308 --> 00:02:54,168
They've got too many over on the right, so that's not an option.

29
00:02:55,168 --> 00:02:55,968
Right now!

30
00:02:56,348 --> 00:02:59,508
This is when I would pass it to him and then run into the goal from the left.

31
00:03:00,508 --> 00:03:00,988
Whoa!

32
00:03:02,048 --> 00:03:03,168
Out on right!

33
00:03:03,168 --> 00:03:07,368
A big moment for Deguchi, who's in the clear!

34
00:03:07,768 --> 00:03:08,968
Oh, nice save!

35
00:03:09,228 --> 00:03:11,208
But what a killer pass from Kuribayashi!

36
00:03:11,868 --> 00:03:12,388
Unbelievable!

37
00:03:14,728 --> 00:03:16,608
His technique really is impressive.

38
00:03:17,068 --> 00:03:17,928
He's also fearless.

39
00:03:18,288 --> 00:03:19,748
That's what truly sets him apart.

40
00:03:20,608 --> 00:03:22,808
For instance, that killer pass he made.

41
00:03:23,028 --> 00:03:26,648
If it had been off by even an inch, the other team would have countered.

42
00:03:26,648 --> 00:03:28,748
But he didn't hesitate for a second.

43
00:03:31,408 --> 00:03:31,888
How?

44
00:03:32,408 --> 00:03:34,448
How is this guy even real?

45
00:03:34,948 --> 00:03:38,128
Aruiza Kuribayashi has only been on the field for five minutes.

46
00:03:38,388 --> 00:03:43,248
But apparently that's all the time he needs to turn the game in his beerion's favor with one touch on the ball!

47
00:03:43,248 --> 00:03:48,448
I'm sorry, man.

48
00:03:49,148 --> 00:03:50,048
I gotta bring it.

49
00:03:50,768 --> 00:03:53,288
Flashy individual plays whenever I get the chance.

50
00:03:54,848 --> 00:03:57,628
I'll still contribute as a member of the team, I swear.

51
00:03:58,048 --> 00:03:59,908
But I have to make the most of this as well.

52
00:04:00,288 --> 00:04:02,288
I need people to remember who I am.

53
00:04:03,288 --> 00:04:05,428
I don't ever want to go back to the bench again.

54
00:04:06,468 --> 00:04:09,228
That's why I have to get every spectator here on my side.

55
00:04:13,248 --> 00:04:18,148
Wow!

56
00:04:18,468 --> 00:04:20,028
That was a close one!

57
00:04:20,768 --> 00:04:22,268
How the heck does he do it?

58
00:04:22,428 --> 00:04:23,788
And how can I be more like him?

59
00:04:24,548 --> 00:04:25,888
His plays are phenomenal.

60
00:04:26,688 --> 00:04:27,088
Unreal.

61
00:04:28,468 --> 00:04:32,108
I was wondering what you would think after watching Kuribayashi play.

62
00:04:32,708 --> 00:04:34,448
And it looks like I have an answer.

63
00:04:35,588 --> 00:04:38,128
I'll remember it from my own feature reference.

64
00:04:39,088 --> 00:04:39,388
Oh?

65
00:04:39,388 --> 00:04:44,348
In this one interview he gave, Kuribayashi said something interesting.

66
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:48,348
Whatever the situation may be, he does the same thing.

67
00:04:48,668 --> 00:04:51,048
Immediately comes up with four viable options.

68
00:04:51,568 --> 00:04:52,888
And then he chooses one.

69
00:04:53,308 --> 00:04:54,188
Four of them?

70
00:04:55,068 --> 00:04:56,588
I don't have options!

71
00:04:56,988 --> 00:04:58,228
I barely have one!

72
00:04:58,448 --> 00:05:01,748
And to be honest, that's really all I can ever handle at any given moment!

73
00:05:02,488 --> 00:05:03,468
Nothing more!

74
00:05:03,948 --> 00:05:05,968
Then you'll have to expand your options.

75
00:05:05,968 --> 00:05:12,108
Listen to me, by watching Kuribayashi's game, you could find something to incorporate into your own.

76
00:05:13,888 --> 00:05:15,028
Take my advice.

77
00:05:15,428 --> 00:05:15,928
Do it.

78
00:05:16,348 --> 00:05:18,448
Or at the very least, give it some thought.

79
00:05:18,448 --> 00:05:40,448
And these are the stars of today's match.

80
00:05:40,448 --> 00:05:43,068
First, we have Deguchi, who scored two times.

81
00:05:43,568 --> 00:05:46,288
And the assist for the winning goal goes to...

82
00:05:46,288 --> 00:05:47,668
Haruhisa Kuribayashi.

83
00:05:48,748 --> 00:05:49,148
What?

84
00:05:49,368 --> 00:05:50,568
Who the heck is this guy?

85
00:05:51,648 --> 00:05:53,248
You know, besides a total monster.

86
00:05:53,248 --> 00:06:08,148
Don't expect him to be as surprised as you are about all this.

87
00:06:08,728 --> 00:06:10,888
We've been watching him play since we were juniors.

88
00:06:11,248 --> 00:06:12,648
We know what he's capable of.

89
00:06:12,648 --> 00:06:19,948
For those of us who joined the academy during grade school, we were usually above average players before we even got here.

90
00:06:21,028 --> 00:06:24,048
We all think we're going to be the top players in junior youth.

91
00:06:24,528 --> 00:06:26,388
I mean, with our backgrounds, how could we not?

92
00:06:27,068 --> 00:06:31,728
But when I saw Kuribayashi on the first day, I immediately thought,

93
00:06:32,408 --> 00:06:35,808
man, guess I'll have to aim to be second best instead.

94
00:06:37,808 --> 00:06:39,828
The number one spot's already taken.

95
00:06:39,828 --> 00:06:44,148
Next, we have Kuribayashi.

96
00:06:45,688 --> 00:06:49,568
Every time we see you in a match, it blows our minds that you're still in high school.

97
00:06:50,128 --> 00:06:51,808
What a fantastic game you had today.

98
00:06:53,708 --> 00:06:58,608
Well, I've been practicing with the first team, so I'm used to this level of play, if I'm being honest.

99
00:06:59,328 --> 00:07:02,528
There was never really a moment where I felt like I couldn't keep up with them.

100
00:07:03,208 --> 00:07:06,088
Well, you are absolutely on par with them, that's for sure.

101
00:07:06,348 --> 00:07:08,248
So are you focusing on physical training?

102
00:07:08,248 --> 00:07:11,468
If you do, your core will get stronger and you'll start bulking up.

103
00:07:11,688 --> 00:07:12,908
And you won't be so thin.

104
00:07:22,728 --> 00:07:24,848
He's like the Bane of all interviewers.

105
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:29,388
When they ask something useless, he just stares them down as if he knows what they're looking for.

106
00:07:30,228 --> 00:07:31,848
Everyone knows he's difficult.

107
00:07:31,848 --> 00:07:35,428
Okay, but how is that question worthless?

108
00:07:35,428 --> 00:07:46,648
The way I see it, someone who talks up their physical training is probably hiding their lack of technique.

109
00:07:47,528 --> 00:07:51,868
So why should I listen to outside opinions when I know what I need better than anyone?

110
00:07:52,368 --> 00:07:57,988
There's only one possible exception to that, and it's Manager Fukuda of the Aspirion Youth Team.

111
00:07:57,988 --> 00:08:00,408
Oh, well, thank you very much.

112
00:08:01,088 --> 00:08:03,868
That's a wrap on our interviews with today's star players.

113
00:08:07,208 --> 00:08:11,528
Yoshitsune, you're starting a different training regimen tomorrow.

114
00:08:13,928 --> 00:08:14,568
Sure.

115
00:08:14,568 --> 00:08:19,788
Okay, aside from those of you who live in the dorms, you're dismissing...

116
00:08:19,788 --> 00:08:24,088
Someone who talks up their physical training is probably hiding their lack of technique.

117
00:08:24,088 --> 00:08:26,148
I get it now.

118
00:08:26,748 --> 00:08:28,428
He wasn't sliding being physical.

119
00:08:28,688 --> 00:08:30,268
He was just stating his priorities.

120
00:08:31,188 --> 00:08:33,468
Technique is more important to him than strength.

121
00:08:33,908 --> 00:08:34,888
Makes sense.

122
00:08:35,448 --> 00:08:37,808
He's clearly confident in his own level of skill.

123
00:08:38,648 --> 00:08:39,228
Amazing.

124
00:08:40,008 --> 00:08:43,348
Everything about Haruhisa Kurabayashi is blowing my mind.

125
00:08:43,768 --> 00:08:44,708
I want to meet him.

126
00:08:45,308 --> 00:08:47,368
No, I don't just want to meet him.

127
00:08:47,368 --> 00:08:52,728
If you want to play with him, then make the A-team and do it as soon as possible.

128
00:08:52,728 --> 00:08:57,468
Kurabayashi will undoubtedly return to the A-team at some point.

129
00:08:57,988 --> 00:09:00,888
The sooner you join, the sooner you can show them your value.

130
00:09:01,188 --> 00:09:05,048
And then hopefully by the time he gets back, the seed will have sprouted.

131
00:09:05,488 --> 00:09:07,528
You'll be able to connect with him as a peer.

132
00:09:08,608 --> 00:09:11,848
But in order to do that, you have to remember what I said earlier...

133
00:09:11,848 --> 00:09:14,688
Adding something from Kurabayashi's game to my own, right?

134
00:09:14,688 --> 00:09:16,908
I know exactly what it is!

135
00:09:17,568 --> 00:09:18,228
You do?

136
00:09:18,788 --> 00:09:19,308
Really?

137
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:24,948
Huh?

138
00:09:26,388 --> 00:09:27,188
Uh...

139
00:09:27,188 --> 00:09:29,988
Where's Hana?

140
00:09:34,408 --> 00:09:34,708
Hmm?

141
00:09:37,708 --> 00:09:38,728
What the...?

142
00:09:38,728 --> 00:09:40,148
Everyone listen up!

143
00:09:40,608 --> 00:09:42,648
Yoshitsune was injured in the match in Aomori.

144
00:09:42,648 --> 00:09:47,428
So we'll be moving some of our front-line players from the B-team over to the A-team.

145
00:09:48,808 --> 00:09:50,688
Fukuda said he'll be at our game this weekend.

146
00:09:51,128 --> 00:09:52,608
He'll be determining who moves up.

147
00:09:52,868 --> 00:09:54,888
This is a huge opportunity for you guys.

148
00:10:02,308 --> 00:10:03,748
I don't know much at all.

149
00:10:05,028 --> 00:10:06,348
About soccer, anyway.

150
00:10:06,348 --> 00:10:13,908
I spent so much time revising these.

151
00:10:14,188 --> 00:10:17,928
He said he wanted to eat whatever he wants, so I tried to make them more palatable.

152
00:10:18,768 --> 00:10:19,728
And then...

153
00:10:19,728 --> 00:10:21,288
I couldn't give them to him.

154
00:10:23,668 --> 00:10:25,188
What am I saying?!

155
00:10:25,188 --> 00:10:27,388
Literally all I had to do was hand them over!

156
00:10:28,728 --> 00:10:29,288
Whatever!

157
00:10:29,928 --> 00:10:30,688
I'm leaving!

158
00:10:30,688 --> 00:10:33,808
You can do it, Ashito.

159
00:10:34,228 --> 00:10:37,608
After that goal you made, moving up to the A-team is a real possibility.

160
00:10:38,608 --> 00:10:39,288
And I promise.

161
00:10:39,828 --> 00:10:42,328
I'll just watch from afar so that I don't get in your way.

162
00:10:45,308 --> 00:10:45,708
Fukuda.

163
00:10:46,488 --> 00:10:47,648
Don't forget what I said.

164
00:10:47,968 --> 00:10:49,288
I'm serious about Aoi.

165
00:10:49,968 --> 00:10:50,588
I think you...

166
00:10:50,588 --> 00:10:51,608
The sooner the better.

167
00:10:54,948 --> 00:10:56,148
Better for him, I mean.

168
00:10:56,148 --> 00:11:02,808
If he can do what he needs to do in the next game, that's faster than I could have imagined.

169
00:11:03,688 --> 00:11:05,128
You've been an excellent guide.

170
00:11:06,008 --> 00:11:06,828
Thank you, Nozomi.

171
00:11:06,828 --> 00:11:07,328
Hmm.

172
00:11:20,788 --> 00:11:21,888
Aw, yeah!

173
00:11:22,888 --> 00:11:25,148
I'm one lucky son of a you-know-what!

174
00:11:25,188 --> 00:11:26,768
I'm playing a match every week!

175
00:11:26,768 --> 00:11:27,708
What's with the screaming?

176
00:11:28,168 --> 00:11:29,868
Where'd you get all this energy, man?

177
00:11:30,128 --> 00:11:31,208
You're obviously tired.

178
00:11:31,368 --> 00:11:32,228
Look at your face!

179
00:11:33,908 --> 00:11:34,808
Hey there, Aoi.

180
00:11:34,808 --> 00:11:37,308
I hear you've been working hard on your night training.

181
00:11:37,568 --> 00:11:39,588
You still practicing kill it, then kick it?

182
00:11:40,148 --> 00:11:41,208
Ha ha ha!

183
00:11:41,688 --> 00:11:44,028
Well, maybe a little, but...

184
00:11:44,028 --> 00:11:45,408
Just you wait and see!

185
00:11:45,568 --> 00:11:48,468
I've learned something awesome from watching Kuribayashi play!

186
00:11:48,648 --> 00:11:49,448
Hey, Aoi!

187
00:11:49,688 --> 00:11:49,848
Huh?

188
00:11:50,208 --> 00:11:51,468
So you ready to do this?

189
00:11:54,068 --> 00:11:54,548
Hmm.

190
00:11:57,388 --> 00:11:57,868
Yeah!

191
00:11:57,868 --> 00:11:57,948
Yeah!

192
00:11:57,948 --> 00:12:16,828
Watch, old man.

193
00:12:17,108 --> 00:12:19,148
I'm moving up to the A-team after this.

194
00:12:19,388 --> 00:12:20,588
Then it's all over!

195
00:12:20,588 --> 00:12:29,528
It's a different team when you're here.

196
00:12:29,648 --> 00:12:30,868
They're suddenly all motivated.

197
00:12:31,248 --> 00:12:31,908
That's so.

198
00:12:33,908 --> 00:12:34,048
Huh?

199
00:12:35,048 --> 00:12:35,528
Otimo!

200
00:12:37,348 --> 00:12:37,828
Move!

201
00:12:37,828 --> 00:12:47,548
They've gotten so much better.

202
00:12:48,048 --> 00:12:49,788
Hard to believe it's only been a week.

203
00:12:50,248 --> 00:12:50,608
Middle.

204
00:12:51,108 --> 00:12:51,288
Hmm.

205
00:12:52,028 --> 00:12:53,608
There's an open space in the middle!

206
00:12:53,908 --> 00:12:55,668
Why are you all getting drawn out?

207
00:12:55,668 --> 00:12:56,188
Ah!

208
00:12:57,648 --> 00:12:59,848
By watching Kuribayashi's game,

209
00:13:00,108 --> 00:13:02,408
you could find something to incorporate into your own.

210
00:13:03,248 --> 00:13:04,508
Take my advice.

211
00:13:04,888 --> 00:13:05,408
Do it.

212
00:13:05,408 --> 00:13:08,888
A killer pass!

213
00:13:11,288 --> 00:13:11,928
Ooh?

214
00:13:12,748 --> 00:13:14,088
What the heck?

215
00:13:15,728 --> 00:13:16,648
Move up!

216
00:13:16,748 --> 00:13:17,128
Come on!

217
00:13:17,148 --> 00:13:17,648
Let's go!

218
00:13:21,828 --> 00:13:22,888
Over there.

219
00:13:23,408 --> 00:13:25,128
Kuribayashi's breaking free for a pass.

220
00:13:25,608 --> 00:13:27,168
So that means I should aim there

221
00:13:27,168 --> 00:13:28,508
so he gets it in midair.

222
00:13:29,228 --> 00:13:30,368
One eye-opening.

223
00:13:30,668 --> 00:13:31,908
Lightning killer pass!

224
00:13:32,008 --> 00:13:32,628
Coming up!

225
00:13:35,408 --> 00:13:36,668
What the crap!

226
00:13:37,368 --> 00:13:39,188
What the hell was that?

227
00:13:39,288 --> 00:13:41,908
Did they tell you which goal you were supposed to be aiming for?

228
00:13:42,268 --> 00:13:42,788
Why?

229
00:13:43,228 --> 00:13:45,628
Why isn't this stupid ball going where I want it?

230
00:13:45,948 --> 00:13:46,108
Uh?

231
00:13:46,588 --> 00:13:46,788
Huh?

232
00:13:46,788 --> 00:13:55,508
I heard that you gave him some great advice at the barbecue place.

233
00:13:55,768 --> 00:13:56,228
That's it?

234
00:13:58,228 --> 00:14:00,828
Because it doesn't really seem to be working out for him.

235
00:14:01,208 --> 00:14:03,908
I do not know what he thinks he's going to accomplish out there,

236
00:14:04,008 --> 00:14:06,028
but his intentions are definitely interesting.

237
00:14:06,028 --> 00:14:07,408
He's going to be making a mistake.

238
00:14:07,408 --> 00:14:07,948
He's going to be making a mistake.

239
00:14:07,948 --> 00:14:08,448
He's going to be making a mistake.

240
00:14:08,448 --> 00:14:10,308
Twice he's made the exact same call.

241
00:14:10,748 --> 00:14:11,908
Without any hesitation,

242
00:14:12,108 --> 00:14:14,368
he's passing to players who are hidden behind opponents.

243
00:14:16,368 --> 00:14:17,248
Excuse me.

244
00:14:17,868 --> 00:14:18,148
Hmm?

245
00:14:18,608 --> 00:14:20,628
Could you possibly tone it down a bit

246
00:14:20,628 --> 00:14:22,148
and not speak to me so much?

247
00:14:24,328 --> 00:14:25,528
Yeah, sure.

248
00:14:26,088 --> 00:14:26,868
Keep it up.

249
00:14:26,868 --> 00:14:39,888
I'm leaving the coaching to Nozomi.

250
00:14:40,428 --> 00:14:41,888
I have just one thing to say,

251
00:14:41,988 --> 00:14:43,768
and then I'll let you all get back to your talk.

252
00:14:44,388 --> 00:14:44,928
Tell me,

253
00:14:45,408 --> 00:14:47,468
why are you looking at us during play?

254
00:14:49,948 --> 00:14:53,188
Are you playing this match against your manager?

255
00:14:54,468 --> 00:14:56,348
Your opponents are in front of you,

256
00:14:56,348 --> 00:14:57,208
on the field.

257
00:14:57,988 --> 00:15:00,008
The positions you're given are yours.

258
00:15:00,568 --> 00:15:01,888
Do not forget that.

259
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:12,988
It's strange.

260
00:15:13,408 --> 00:15:15,268
Everyone seems a lot calmer now.

261
00:15:15,668 --> 00:15:17,928
Were they really looking over at the bench during the game?

262
00:15:22,048 --> 00:15:24,588
You're the one who should be watching me, old man.

263
00:15:25,008 --> 00:15:25,488
An alley.

264
00:15:26,348 --> 00:15:27,308
Uh, yeah.

265
00:15:28,528 --> 00:15:29,768
Imitation isn't enough.

266
00:15:30,268 --> 00:15:31,908
If you want to play like Kurabayashi,

267
00:15:32,068 --> 00:15:33,508
then you should think about his movements.

268
00:15:34,808 --> 00:15:36,028
A pass is a pass,

269
00:15:36,108 --> 00:15:37,768
whether it's a so-called killer pass

270
00:15:37,768 --> 00:15:39,168
or a short pass.

271
00:15:39,388 --> 00:15:41,448
It's just a means of getting to the goal.

272
00:15:42,728 --> 00:15:44,268
Those were supposed to be passes.

273
00:15:44,608 --> 00:15:46,308
Wait, that's what he was doing?

274
00:15:46,448 --> 00:15:47,388
I'm so confused.

275
00:15:47,388 --> 00:15:51,808
A pass is a pass.

276
00:15:51,808 --> 00:15:53,568
A means of getting to the goal.

277
00:15:56,848 --> 00:15:57,748
Oh, wow.

278
00:15:58,388 --> 00:15:59,408
I get it now.

279
00:16:02,688 --> 00:16:05,348
That means it should go there.

280
00:16:05,608 --> 00:16:07,908
If this pass works...

281
00:16:07,908 --> 00:16:08,468
Ultimo!

282
00:16:11,588 --> 00:16:13,008
He broke through on the right.

283
00:16:14,268 --> 00:16:14,748
Easy.

284
00:16:14,868 --> 00:16:16,748
Just block the shooting angle and we're good.

285
00:16:19,508 --> 00:16:21,088
Guess I can't get to the middle now.

286
00:16:21,088 --> 00:16:22,828
I know it's due.

287
00:16:29,548 --> 00:16:29,828
It's...

288
00:16:29,828 --> 00:16:30,548
It's...

289
00:16:30,548 --> 00:16:31,548
It's...

290
00:16:31,548 --> 00:16:43,928
Ashito's a weird kid.

291
00:16:44,108 --> 00:16:46,428
I never expected him to score a goal like that.

292
00:16:46,848 --> 00:16:48,148
A pass is just a pass

293
00:16:48,148 --> 00:16:50,048
and a means of getting to the goal to score.

294
00:16:50,488 --> 00:16:50,728
Wow.

295
00:16:51,588 --> 00:16:53,468
Nice choice of words, Coach Nozomi.

296
00:16:53,468 --> 00:16:57,728
What type of goal are you envisioning

297
00:16:57,728 --> 00:16:59,568
when you pass the ball to another player?

298
00:17:00,428 --> 00:17:03,128
A killer pass isn't killer until you can answer that.

299
00:17:03,728 --> 00:17:05,948
You want to know what impressed me the most just now?

300
00:17:06,328 --> 00:17:08,268
He envisioned himself scoring a goal

301
00:17:08,268 --> 00:17:10,268
and worked backwards to make it a reality.

302
00:17:11,548 --> 00:17:14,228
I'm Gabriel Batistuta, reincarnated!

303
00:17:14,608 --> 00:17:15,608
I have returned!

304
00:17:15,968 --> 00:17:18,028
And yes, I realize he's still alive!

305
00:17:18,868 --> 00:17:21,348
Improving the precision of my passes is a given.

306
00:17:21,348 --> 00:17:24,348
But what's most important to me is scoring.

307
00:17:24,848 --> 00:17:25,688
I'm a forward!

308
00:17:25,988 --> 00:17:27,868
And that's our ultimate drive!

309
00:17:29,288 --> 00:17:30,008
Nozomi,

310
00:17:30,508 --> 00:17:32,708
can you call him to the clubhouse later?

311
00:17:33,548 --> 00:17:34,748
I'll tell him myself.

312
00:17:39,208 --> 00:17:39,928
Understood.

313
00:17:42,588 --> 00:17:44,148
I'm coming in!

314
00:17:47,348 --> 00:17:47,948
Hm.

315
00:17:51,348 --> 00:17:55,968
A sweeping three-to-zero victory.

316
00:17:56,508 --> 00:17:57,288
Well done.

317
00:17:57,728 --> 00:17:58,668
This was all you.

318
00:17:59,728 --> 00:18:01,128
You made me do it.

319
00:18:01,868 --> 00:18:02,188
Huh?

320
00:18:04,508 --> 00:18:06,728
I'm loving soccer more each day.

321
00:18:07,348 --> 00:18:09,348
There are so many things I can do now

322
00:18:09,348 --> 00:18:10,468
that I couldn't do before.

323
00:18:10,868 --> 00:18:13,908
Best part is that there is still a ton more left to learn.

324
00:18:14,428 --> 00:18:14,628
Hm.

325
00:18:14,628 --> 00:18:17,688
I am in such a good place right now.

326
00:18:18,008 --> 00:18:19,928
And it's all because I met you.

327
00:18:20,488 --> 00:18:21,508
Thanks, old man.

328
00:18:24,408 --> 00:18:26,248
Will you move me to the A-team?

329
00:18:27,348 --> 00:18:30,648
I'm not saying I'd be able to replace Yoshitsune right away.

330
00:18:30,988 --> 00:18:32,928
I still have such a long way to go.

331
00:18:33,528 --> 00:18:34,008
But I...

332
00:18:34,008 --> 00:18:36,448
I can do this!

333
00:18:36,748 --> 00:18:37,708
I'll get better!

334
00:18:37,708 --> 00:18:43,268
We haven't spoken alone in a while, huh?

335
00:18:43,648 --> 00:18:45,188
Not since the beach, I think.

336
00:18:46,328 --> 00:18:47,468
I'm sorry, Ashito.

337
00:18:48,068 --> 00:18:49,668
I can't promote you just yet.

338
00:18:50,108 --> 00:18:50,428
Huh?

339
00:18:51,288 --> 00:18:52,248
You can't?

340
00:18:52,348 --> 00:18:52,948
But why?

341
00:18:53,388 --> 00:18:53,888
Ashito,

342
00:18:54,888 --> 00:18:57,168
turn yourself into a defender.

343
00:18:58,868 --> 00:19:01,028
I could be more precise, couldn't I?

344
00:19:01,448 --> 00:19:01,988
All right.

345
00:19:01,988 --> 00:19:04,508
When you finally play on the world stage,

346
00:19:04,688 --> 00:19:05,828
it'll be as a fullback.

347
00:19:20,248 --> 00:19:23,208
You want me to be a defender?

348
00:19:23,968 --> 00:19:25,628
I don't understand what you're saying.

349
00:19:25,908 --> 00:19:26,388
Why?

350
00:19:27,128 --> 00:19:29,528
Your skills are better suited for that position.

351
00:19:29,528 --> 00:19:32,128
You will never again play as a forward.

352
00:19:33,068 --> 00:19:35,148
A complete transition.

353
00:19:36,128 --> 00:19:36,488
No!

354
00:19:37,328 --> 00:19:38,508
Wait a sec.

355
00:19:39,328 --> 00:19:39,748
I...

356
00:19:39,748 --> 00:19:41,408
I'm a forward.

357
00:19:41,888 --> 00:19:42,628
Are...

358
00:19:42,628 --> 00:19:45,528
Are you saying...

359
00:19:46,348 --> 00:19:48,328
that my play as a forward is no good?

360
00:19:49,208 --> 00:19:50,448
That's who I am.

361
00:19:51,328 --> 00:19:53,408
I did so well during this game!

362
00:19:53,948 --> 00:19:54,988
I know I did!

363
00:19:55,248 --> 00:19:56,468
And in the last one!

364
00:19:56,988 --> 00:19:59,268
You did, and I'm not denying that.

365
00:19:59,528 --> 00:20:01,168
Do you want to know why, though?

366
00:20:01,828 --> 00:20:03,508
Because of your natural gift.

367
00:20:04,148 --> 00:20:04,508
What?

368
00:20:05,328 --> 00:20:07,828
And that gift cannot be put to best use

369
00:20:07,828 --> 00:20:08,988
if you're on the front line.

370
00:20:09,648 --> 00:20:11,888
By grasping the situation from the back,

371
00:20:12,108 --> 00:20:12,548
you'll be...

372
00:20:12,548 --> 00:20:14,168
I don't get what you're trying to say!

373
00:20:14,288 --> 00:20:14,568
No!

374
00:20:14,648 --> 00:20:15,508
I don't want to!

375
00:20:15,808 --> 00:20:17,708
I came here because I want to become

376
00:20:17,708 --> 00:20:19,228
the best forward in the world!

377
00:20:19,628 --> 00:20:20,968
So then I owe it to you

378
00:20:20,968 --> 00:20:22,588
to tell you why that'll never happen.

379
00:20:23,468 --> 00:20:25,848
First, the ball doesn't stay at your feet.

380
00:20:27,168 --> 00:20:28,908
That won't cut it on the A-team.

381
00:20:29,508 --> 00:20:30,968
Then I'll go practice more!

382
00:20:31,028 --> 00:20:32,628
I don't have any problems going late!

383
00:20:32,668 --> 00:20:33,528
You are not agile.

384
00:20:33,808 --> 00:20:34,988
There is no power at all

385
00:20:34,988 --> 00:20:36,008
in your short sprints.

386
00:20:36,528 --> 00:20:37,668
You're a slow mess

387
00:20:37,668 --> 00:20:38,908
after the first 10 meters.

388
00:20:39,568 --> 00:20:41,448
These things are fatal as a forward.

389
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:46,768
You do have a keen eye for scoring.

390
00:20:47,208 --> 00:20:49,128
However, you don't have the ability

391
00:20:49,128 --> 00:20:49,968
to back it up.

392
00:20:53,008 --> 00:20:54,708
This isn't about the environment

393
00:20:54,708 --> 00:20:55,468
that you're in.

394
00:20:55,748 --> 00:20:57,288
It's not because you joined late.

395
00:20:57,908 --> 00:20:59,348
It's a part of what's you.

396
00:21:00,568 --> 00:21:01,928
At the moment you were born,

397
00:21:02,048 --> 00:21:03,988
it had already been decided for you.

398
00:21:04,888 --> 00:21:06,768
You were not meant to be a forward.

399
00:21:06,768 --> 00:21:11,168
This was my plan from the start

400
00:21:11,168 --> 00:21:13,428
when I first met you in Aimee.

401
00:21:14,508 --> 00:21:16,648
I had a vacant hole at fullback

402
00:21:16,648 --> 00:21:17,328
in my vision

403
00:21:17,328 --> 00:21:18,988
and I knew you could fill it

404
00:21:18,988 --> 00:21:21,788
like a missing puzzle piece.

405
00:21:22,388 --> 00:21:24,048
What the hell are you saying?

406
00:21:24,388 --> 00:21:25,948
If you knew I couldn't be a forward,

407
00:21:26,108 --> 00:21:27,248
why didn't you tell me?

408
00:21:27,428 --> 00:21:28,628
Why wait till now?

409
00:21:28,888 --> 00:21:30,308
You wouldn't have come if I did.

410
00:21:32,168 --> 00:21:33,988
This was the best time to do it.

411
00:21:36,768 --> 00:21:39,068
No, I don't want to be a defender.

412
00:21:39,348 --> 00:21:39,828
Please.

413
00:21:40,568 --> 00:21:41,648
Please, old man.

414
00:21:41,948 --> 00:21:42,508
Please, no.

415
00:21:42,908 --> 00:21:44,268
If it's not what you want,

416
00:21:44,948 --> 00:21:46,748
then you're certainly free to leave.

417
00:21:47,428 --> 00:21:48,888
We can't hold onto players

418
00:21:48,888 --> 00:21:50,548
we know will never be good enough.

419
00:21:50,548 --> 00:21:50,608
Oh.

420
00:22:06,768 --> 00:22:11,188
IE

421
00:22:14,428 --> 00:22:15,928
Owie...

422
00:22:17,528 --> 00:22:19,948
...

423
00:22:19,948 --> 00:22:21,268
...

424
00:22:21,268 --> 00:22:21,948
...

425
00:22:21,948 --> 00:22:23,328
...

426
00:22:23,328 --> 00:22:23,788
...

427
00:22:23,788 --> 00:22:25,528
...

428
00:22:25,528 --> 00:22:27,768
...

429
00:22:27,768 --> 00:22:28,768
...

430
00:22:28,768 --> 00:22:29,228
...

431
00:22:29,228 --> 00:22:29,668
...

432
00:22:29,668 --> 00:22:30,648
...

433
00:22:30,648 --> 00:23:00,628
Thank you.

434
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,346
Next time on Awashi, it's just soccer.

